  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cooler and dry today behind the front. \n\nA cool northwest flow and associated upslope flow and shallow lake \ninduced instability will support plenty of cloud cover, maybe even a \npassing shower through at least midday today, with only \npartial/gradual clearing in the afternoon. Temperatures will be much \ncooler than the past few days but very close to average for the end \nof October.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Another extended period of dry weather and above \naverage temperatures this weekend through early next week.\n\nSurface high pressure will settle over the eastern Great Lakes \nSaturday, then gradually drift off the southern New England coast \nSunday through Monday. This feature will maintain dry weather across \nthe eastern Great Lakes with temperatures trending above average.\n\nA more active pattern may develop by the middle to end of next week \nas a deep trough moves slowly east across the CONUS, possibly \nevolving into a closed low as it reaches the Ohio Valley and Great \nLakes. There is considerable spread in ensemble members and \ndeterministic model runs with the timing of this system, but once it \narrives it will likely bring a wetter pattern that lasts for at \nleast a few days later next week.",
